Quoting  Raisse the Thaumaturge  <raisse@valdyas.org>:
>blipster8 wrote:
>>Any successful prayer counts against your prayer timeout; 
>Doesn't unsuccessful prayer count against your prayer timeout, too? I've
>always thought it was *worse* for your prayer timeout than successful
>prayer. 

angrygods() gives you u.ublesscnt = rnz(300), which is all results from
"<god> seems displeased" on down. A successful pray, including one where
your god is pleased but not enough to do anything, sets it to rnz(350).
However, only in the latter case is it increased by rnz(1000) for crowning
and again for having killed Rodney.

Rehumanisation of undead by lawful gods doesn't change the prayer timeout
at all that I can see. Neither does prayer in Gehennom. Praying too soon
gives you an extra rnz(250) (but if it was also a crossaligned altar prayer,
you get angrygods() and the base rnz(300) from that); praying while too
naughty or unlucky gets you angrygods; praying at a crossaligned altar (but
not too soon) gets you an extra rnz(250) but actually I think that always
means a trip to angrygods().

So generally unsuccessful prayers count, but for less, and for much less
once crowned and/or Rodney is dead.
